The closest model for adding a `capacityWarning` is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignBulkSignupWarning.java` — an `Assign*` function that counts existing owners and sets a boolean warning flag on the `Owner` (`owner.setBulkSignupWarning(...)`). A new `Assign...` step would slot into the pipeline (after `BuildOwner`, like the other `Assign*` steps) and be wired into `owners.POST.yml`.

## 4. Existing tests for capacity / city owner counts / capacityWarning

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (lines 7-19) — this test currently expects behavior that is **not yet implemented**:

```java
7  /** capacity-warning: 'capacityWarning' is true when the owner's city already holds 40-49
8   * owners (approaching the 50 hard limit). Fill a fresh city to 40, then the next owner in it warns. */
9  class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
11      @Test
12      void coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity() throws Exception {
13          String city = "Warn" + seq();
14          fillCity(city, 40);
15          ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
16          o.put("city", city);
